  "summary": "1980s-reviving electronic music and art: neon grids, chrome sunsets, Testarossa dashes and VHS cop-drama mood.",
  "description": "Synthwave artists (Kavinsky, College, Perturbator) resurrected 1980s soundtrack synthesizers — Tangerine Dream, Jan Hammer — while its artwork codified an 80s that never quite existed: chrome lettering, laser-grid horizons, palm trees, DeLorean dashes. Drive (2011) and Stranger Things mainstreamed it. Divisions: outrun (driving), darksynth (horror), dreamscape. It is the definitive neon-retro reference for games, design and music.",
